  "steps": [
    "In a bowl, combine the pork, green onions, ginger, garlic, oyster sauce, pepper, chili crisp, soy sauce, sesame oil and rice vinegar. Mix until fully combined.",
    "Using a 1 1/2 to 2 tbsp cookie scoop, place mounds of filling in a large nonstick skillet with a lid (or on a sheet pan), leaving space between each one.",
    "Drape a wrapper over each mound and pinch the edges around the filling so it hugs the sides.",
    "Drizzle the avocado oil around the dumplings and set the skillet over medium heat. Pour in the broth, cover, and steam 10 minutes, until the pork reaches 160°F.",
    "Top with soy sauce, chili crisp, green onion and sesame seeds, and serve with rice."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "The fastest homemade dumplings: no folding, on the table in under 25 minutes.",
    "If the pan goes dry before the pork is done, add 2 tbsp water and cover again. Spend With Pennies and Weelicious steam theirs in 2/3 cup water and uncover at the end to crisp the bottoms.",
    "If they do not all fit in one skillet, cook in two batches, splitting the oil and broth."
  ],
